.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1030 AM PDT Thu Oct 1 2026

Patchy LIFR conditions persist over OAK and HAF while VFR
conditions have returned to other terminals. Expecting VFR
conditions to persist with an increase in onshore winds by the
afternoon and early evening hours. Expecting similar conditions as
this morning tonight and into Friday as the marine layer looks to
hold around 1,000 feet in depth. Stratus and/or fog will begin to
dissipate by mid-morning on Friday with an increase in onshore
winds.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Onshore winds increase up to around 15 kt
this afternoon before easing late in the evening. The greatest
probability of seeing sub-MVFR will be between 12Z-17Z Friday,
thus have included it in the official forecast at this time.

SFO Bridge Approach...Greater probability of sub-MVFR between
12Z- 17Z Friday. Otherwise, similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Onshore winds increase this
afternoon before easing after sunset. There is high confidence for
sub-IFR ceilings and/or patchy fog to develop late this evening
and persist into early Friday morning. Southerly winds are likely
at SNS Friday morning before switching onshore by early afternoon.

