.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 1224 PM PDT Thu Oct 1 2026

Persistent ridging across the western United States leaves the
interior hot and dry with poor to very poor daytime humidity
retention away from the immediate coast, while a compressed marine
layer leaves overnight humidity recoveries poor across the higher
elevations. Hot daytime temperatures and mild overnight lows in
the thermal belts pose hazards for fire crews working in high
elevation areas, particularly within the Timber Fire where Major
to Extreme HeatRisk is possible during the weekend. In
addition, the hot and dry conditions lead to rising ERC values
with values in the North Bay and interior Central Coast expected
to reach the 90th to 97th percentile next week.

